# incorrect behavior when started  = 0

- Source URL: https://github.com/taichi-ishitani/tvip-common/issues/3

Hi Taichi! I tried to create stop clk during simulation. 

I have this dependencies in interface
```
    tvip_clock_if gm_clk_if();
    assign gm_clk_if.started = (clk_en == 1) ? 1 : 0 ;
```

So, when clk_en = 0   ->   gm_clk_if.started = 0 

I see figure below  
![Screenshot_bad](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/35744340/208059355-0a134b3e-4209-4e2c-b15e-6038418ad5f7.png)

As you can see, clk change value after clk_en = 0.

I think it's not good behaviour. The main reason of it 

https://github.com/taichi-ishitani/tvip-common/blob/master/src/tvip_clock_if.sv#L36

 ```
 always @(posedge started) begin
    while (started) begin
      #(half_period);                                            <---
      clk ^= 1;
    end
  end
```


the delay should be after the after `clk ^= 1;`

 ```
 always @(posedge started) begin
    while (started) begin
      clk ^= 1;
      #(half_period);
    end
  end
```

In this case figure below 
